  "slug": "single-nucleotide-precision-67f0",
  "summary": "New preprints detect tissue-derived somatic mutations and clonal mosaicism from plasma, and refine InDel signatures in 887 myeloma genomes.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is measuring somatic change in tissue without direct sampling or at finer mutational resolution. Two cfDNA preprints report that ultra-sensitive plasma sequencing detects clonal mosaicism and liver-derived somatic mutations in chronic liver disease, with ulcerative colitis also covered for mosaicism; the liver study reports etiology-linked patterns and a reduction after intervention. A refined InDel taxonomy applied to 887 multiple myeloma whole genomes broadens the repertoire of mutational processes, identifies a TXNDC5 hotspot, and links signatures to treatment outcome. A benchmark of sample mispairing detection tools in multimodal cancer datasets addresses sample-identity quality control rather than mutagenesis. FiberTron and the TNBC Perturb-seq network study concern regulatory variant effects and gene regulatory inference, adjacent to the mutational theme.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-27"
}
